# Copy this file to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill in real values for local `wrangler dev`.
# Never commit `.dev.vars` or real secret values.
#
# In production these are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`, except
# ALLOWED_ORIGIN and WORKER_HOST, which are plain [vars] in wrangler.toml.
# See docs/self-hosting.md.

SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=replace-with-anon-key
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=replace-with-service-role-key
OPENAI_API_KEY=replace-with-openai-api-key

# Optional, and needed for the Claude models in the catalogue. Without it an
# agent set to a `claude-*` model answers with an error naming this variable
# rather than a 401 from Anthropic — `lib/completion.ts` checks first on
# purpose. Also what `worker/eval/` reads: every case in that eval is a Claude
# model, and it looks here before it looks anywhere else.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. Sends completions to an OpenAI-compatible endpoint instead of
# OpenAI. Set OPENAI_MODEL alongside it — the shipped model list is OpenAI's,
# so on its own every agent would ask your endpoint for `gpt-4o`. Transcription
# still goes to OpenAI; docs/self-hosting.md says why.
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# OPENAI_MODEL=llama3.3:70b

# Optional, and separate from the two above on purpose: this is where the text
# of every uploaded document goes, which is a bigger decision than where the
# conversation goes, so it does not inherit from OPENAI_BASE_URL.
# EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS must match both the model and the width
# document_chunks.embedding was declared with — 1536 unless you ran
# supabase/optional/embedding_width.sql, which is also where the procedure for
# changing it lives.
# EMBEDDING_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# EMBEDDING_MODEL=nomic-embed-text
# EMBEDDING_DIMENSIONS=768

# Optional. Cosine-similarity floor for retrieval; unset means 0.25, which was
# tuned for text-embedding-3-small. Set your own if you change the embedding
# model — a wrong floor does not error, it just returns the wrong chunks.
# RAG_MIN_SIMILARITY=0.3

# Optional. Turns retrieval's keyword-matching arm on or off; unset or "on"
# means enabled. Turn it "off" for a corpus that isn't Turkish or English —
# the matching has no dictionary behind it and can add noise without adding
# recall on a corpus it wasn't tuned for.
# RAG_LEXICAL=off

# Comma-separated EXACT frontend origins. Never a wildcard or a pattern —
# docs/self-hosting.md explains what that costs. localhost is allowed in code.
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# 32 random bytes, base64: `openssl rand -base64 32`
# Must decode to exactly 16, 24 or 32 bytes (AES-GCM), and must be byte-identical
# to the routine engine's copy — the API encrypts delivery secrets with it and
# the engine decrypts them.
ROUTINE_SECRET_KEY=

# Email delivery for routines. Leave blank to disable it.
RESEND_API_KEY=
RESEND_FROM=

# Optional. How many third-party events (a new mail, a Slack message) may start
# one routine in an hour and in a day before it is paused and its owner told.
# A fuse against a filter that is too wide, not a budget. Defaults: 60 and 500.
# ROUTINE_EVENT_RUNS_PER_HOUR=60
# ROUTINE_EVENT_RUNS_PER_DAY=500

# Optional. This Worker's own domain, for the routine engine's SSRF guard. Leave
# unset on workers.dev — that whole domain class is already blocked.
# WORKER_HOST=api.example.com

# Optional. Shared secret for POST /admin/backfill-embeddings, sent in the
# `x-admin-key` header. Unset, that endpoint fails closed.
# ADMIN_API_KEY=

# Optional. Connected apps — about fifteen hundred applications an agent can
# search, and the ones somebody has connected it can call. Unset, the feature is
# not offered and the Integrations page names this variable. Get one at
# dashboard.composio.dev, and read docs/integrations.md first: it adds a
# subprocessor, it bills per call, and the page that collects a user's key
# carries Composio's branding until you set your own.
# COMPOSIO_API_KEY=
# Optional, with the key above. Lets a routine start on an event in a connected
# app — a new Gmail or Outlook mail, a calendar event about to start. It is the
# signing secret of the project's webhook subscription, which
# `bun run scripts/composio-webhook-subscribe.ts https://<api host>` makes and
# prints. Set it on the cron Worker too: that one makes the triggers, and both
# must agree that events exist. See docs/integrations.md.
# COMPOSIO_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# Routines that start on a Notion page event: the verification_token Notion
# sent to /notion/events (logged while this is unset). Set it on the cron Worker
# too. See docs/integrations.md.
# NOTION_WEBHOOK_VERIFICATION_TOKEN=

# Optional. Lets an agent drive a real browser — read a page that needs
# JavaScript, pull a number out of a site with no API — through browser-use,
# which runs the browser and the agent loop. Unset, the `browse` tool is not
# offered and the Integrations page names this variable.
#
# Four things to know before you set it:
#   1. It adds a subprocessor. A task's instruction, and whatever the browser
#      reads on somebody's behalf, go to browser-use. See docs/security.md.
#   2. YOU pay, not the person asking. There is no per-member key here: one
#      deployment key, billed to you. A self-hosted install charges nobody
#      credits, which here means unbounded: watch the provider's bill. Each
#      run is capped at the provider by maxCostUsd.
#   3. SET IT ON THE CRON WORKER TOO. While the conversation is open in a tab,
#      the tab settles the run; the cron Worker is the fallback for a closed
#      tab, and it also stops a browser somebody walked away from. A key set
#      here and not there starts tasks whose answers never arrive once the tab
#      is closed — and the only sign is a line in `wrangler tail`.
#   4. THE KEY MUST BE FROM A PROJECT WITHOUT ZERO DATA RETENTION. The browser
#      runs on browser-use's V4 API (the same key as v2), and the provider
#      answers 403 "Zero Data Retention is enabled on the project (V4
#      unsupported)" to a project that has it on.
# BROWSER_USE_API_KEY=
# Optional. The model a browser run asks for. Unset means gpt-5.6-luna, the
# default in src/lib/browser/v4.ts.
# BROWSER_USE_MODEL=
# Optional. How hard that model reasons: none, low, medium, high, xhigh, max,
# or `provider` for browser-use's own default (xhigh on gpt-5.6-luna). Unset
# means medium, DEFAULT_REASONING in src/lib/browser/v4.ts.
# BROWSER_USE_REASONING=
# Optional. A proxy in front of api.browser-use.com/api/v4, where runs, browsers
# and profiles go. Unset means browser-use.
# BROWSER_USE_V4_BASE_URL=
# Optional, and V2 ONLY: not consulted for any V4 request. It still carries the
# v2 tasks created before the move to V4 (drained until none are left) and the
# account headroom check, because /billing/account exists only on v2.
# BROWSER_USE_BASE_URL=

# Not set here: DOCS_DIR. Document storage on Cloudflare is the DOCS R2 binding
# declared in wrangler.toml; DOCS_DIR is the Node/Docker filesystem fallback and
# is set by docker-compose.yml, not by this file.
